  "document": "Josh Carter\nJoshua Neville Carter (born November 20, 1986) is an American professional basketball player for Limoges CSP of the LNB Pro A. He played college basketball for Texas A&M. He also played for the Athletes in Action basketball team in 2006 and 2007, helping the team win the William Jones Cup in 2006. In the 2006–07 season, Carter co-led all NCAA Division I men's basketball players with his three-point accuracy of 50%. The 98–37 team record he compiled during his college career makes him the winningest men's basketball player in the program's history."
